  "limitations": [
    "One measured publication per size; these are elapsed observations without CPU isolation, not distributions or an API SLA.",
    "Local time includes input patch validation, bounded final-graph validation and local SQL/repartition; baseline local is full normalization+indexing. Copy, global hash, full integrity, legacy and publication are included in total.",
    "RSS is process high-water mark including initial full build and validation; baseline validates binary with a joined buffer while final benchmark streams SHA-256. Do not interpret their RSS difference as a writer RAM improvement.",
    "Sampled disk covers named files under private benchmark directory during patch, excludes initial build window and unlinked binary spools and may miss brief peaks. Disk usage is recorded, without a predeclared pass threshold.",
    "Incremental publication retains SQLite free pages and additive indexes; its published artifact is larger than baseline. No VACUUM is hidden in local update.",
    "The measured fixture touches 1000 rows, not the maximum allowed 65536-row/64MiB affected region. Graph/moves/split/merge are independent regressions, not million-row timing acceptance.",
    "Atomicity tests cover process failures before/after rename. Power-loss durability and distributed/network filesystems are not accepted.",
    "Old schema-2 readers remain compatible; missing incremental capability requires explicit O(N) rebuild. Normal startup/offline DB migration and complete 3.7-B remain open.",
    "Pre-final 100k run excluded: it preceded oversized no-op payload preflight fix. Recorded final 100k and 1m runs share final production hashes."
